{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\n\nThe outbound comment sync re-posted duplicate comments to Jira on every hourly pass\n(bug `irongrey-chubby-oxpecker` / `aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615`: the PRIMARY comment-id dedup map\n`comment_ids` is inert/empty, leaving only the lossy body-membership fallback). The\nreconcile-bridge workflow is **paused** (`disabled_manually`, confirmed via the Actions API),\nso the duplicate set is FIXED and no longer growing. **REB-1861** is pinned at Jira's\n5000-comment HARD cap, so new comments on it fail with `COMMENTS_PER_ISSUE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED`.\nThis ticket purges the accumulated duplicates.\n\nSame failure class, different route, as bug `1f3d-cb66-d3fc-4356`; its cleanup task\n`bd80-0603-7d44-4d9f` is the established precedent, whose mechanism is reused here.\n\n## How the affected-issue set is enumerated (deterministic, not a guess)\n\nThe set is derived from the LAST reconcile pass before the pause — Actions run **32403944666** of\n`.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml` (2026-08-20T18:34Z). Every touched issue emits\n`RECON: outbound_update key=<KEY> changed=[...] comments=<N>`; the affected set is exactly the keys\nwith `comments>0`. Reproduce with:\n\n```\ngh run view 32403944666 --log \\\n  | grep -oE \"RECON: outbound_update key=[A-Z]+-[0-9]+ changed=\\[[^]]*\\] comments=[0-9]+\" \\\n  | sed -E 's/.*key=([A-Z]+-[0-9]+).*comments=([0-9]+)/\\1 \\2/' | awk '$2>0'\n```\n\nThat yields **30 issues** (the bug ticket's \"~28\" estimate). Keys with `comments=0` in that pass\nare converged and cannot be carrying duplicates from this bug: the body-membership fallback is\ndeterministic, so an issue that matches today matched on every prior pass. The enumerated list is\nthe completeness baseline for the run, is written to an artifact, and drives the script; the\nrun is REFUSED if the key list and the artifact disagree.\n\nMeasured damage (read-only dry run over that list; all 30 passed the completeness check):\n\nThe full 30-row per-issue table is recorded as a comment on this ticket (artifact\n`/Users/joeoakhart/jira-cleanup-20260820/logs/dryrun-all.txt`).\n\n**Totals: 31,683 Jira comments; 30,847 bot-marked; 836 unmarked; 836 distinct bodies kept;\n30,011 duplicates to delete.**\n\n## Mechanism (reused from bd80 — see that ticket for the full rationale)\n\n- **Bot identification — the safety-critical filter. Marker detection runs on the PRE-STRIP\n  rendered text.** A comment is a deletion candidate IFF\n  `adf.adf_to_text(comment[\"body\"])` — the raw ADF→text render, with NO marker strip — contains\n  `RECONCILER_MARKER = \"<!-- rebar:reconciler-echo -->\"` (`outbound_comments.py`, appended by\n  `_decorate_outbound_comment`). This is deliberately NOT `_normalize_comment_body`, which\n  STRIPS the marker before returning and therefore can never be used for detection. The two uses\n  are kept separate and explicit:\n  *detection* = `adf.adf_to_text(body)` (pre-strip);\n  *dedup grouping* = `_normalize_comment_body(body)` (post-strip).\n  A comment whose pre-strip rendered text lacks the marker is treated as foreign and is NEVER a\n  deletion candidate in phase 1.\n- **Secondary cross-check.** All candidates on an issue must resolve to a single bot `author.accountId`; divergence aborts that issue. Observed homogeneous: `712020:6471376f-4e5e-4ed2-8c05-330827bc387e` (the accountId bd80 recorded).\n- **Dedup key = the reconciler's OWN normalization.** Group candidates by\n  `outbound_comments._normalize_comment_body(body)`, imported and reused verbatim, so \"distinct\n  body\" means exactly what the reconciler means by it.\n- **Keep-one rule.** Per distinct normalized body: keep the OLDEST copy (min `created`), delete\n  the rest. A body with only ONE copy is NEVER deleted. This structurally guarantees the\n  invariant that every distinct body retains exactly one instance.\n- **Pagination + completeness gate.** All comments are fetched via\n  `GET /rest/api/3/issue/{key}/comment?startAt=..&maxResults=100&orderBy=created` and the count\n  is reconciled against the `total` from `?maxResults=0`. `len(fetched) != total` REFUSES that\n  issue (guards a silently truncated fetch producing a dangerous delete list).\n- **Rate limiting — 429 IS retried, explicitly.** DELETE does NOT go through\n  `delete_comment`/`_direct_rest_delete`, which re-raise 4xx/5xx immediately and would hard-abort\n  on the first 429 across ~30k calls. Every request goes through the script's own wrapper, which\n  honours `Retry-After` on 429 and backs off exponentially on 5xx/transient faults, plus a\n  per-call throttle. A 404 on DELETE is idempotent success, so re-runs are safe.\n- **Append-only deletion log** (`/Users/joeoakhart/jira-cleanup-20260820/logs/deletions.jsonl`: key, id, body hash, outcome, ts) flushed per deletion, so a stalled run is resumable.\n\n### Phase 2 — the 836 truncation-suffix comments (separate, evidence-gated)\n\nThree issues (REB-1567: 418, REB-1931: 278, REB-2605: 140) carry comments with NO marker. They are\nnot human: same bot accountId, repeated ~139x identically, rendered text ending in\n`_TRUNCATION_SUFFIX = \" … [truncated by reconciler]\"` (`adapters/jira/comment_limits.py`) — the\nreconciler's own outbound truncation, which cut the 32767-char body short and removed the trailing\nmarker paragraph. Because the phase-1 authoritative identifier is absent, these run as a SEPARATE\nphase behind `--include-truncated`, with its own dry run, under the rule: rendered text ends with\n`_TRUNCATION_SUFFIX` AND `author.accountId` == the resolved bot accountId. Keep-one still applies,\nso the one-surviving-copy invariant is unchanged. Phase 2 is not needed to clear the cap.\n\n## Safety plan (T4 — irreversible)\n\n- [x] **Pre-deletion backup** of the FULL comment payload (id, ADF body, author accountId +\n      display name, created) per issue, written and completeness-checked BEFORE any DELETE.\n- [x] **Dry-run default.** Deletion requires an explicit `--execute`. The dry run prints, per\n      issue: fetched/reported total, marked count, unmarked count, distinct-body count, the kept\n      id per body, and the delete count, and writes a per-issue machine-readable plan artifact.\n- [x] **Canary first.** Execute on ONE light issue, verify it fully, then proceed.\n      **REB-1861 runs LAST** (largest and riskiest).\n- [x] **Per-issue post-verification**: re-fetch and assert every distinct normalized body present\n      before the run still has exactly one surviving copy, that the unmarked count is unchanged,\n      and that the issue is below the cap.\n- [x] Ambiguous cases are SKIPPED and reported, never guessed.\n- [x] The reconcile-bridge workflow stays PAUSED for the whole operation and is NOT re-enabled\n      by this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] [non-codebase] provenance: GitHub Actions run 32403944666 + operator-local artifacts under\n      /Users/joeoakhart/jira-cleanup-20260820/ (OUTSIDE this repository; nothing cited here is repo-resident).\n      Affected-issue list derived by the documented command from run 32403944666,\n      written as an artifact, and the run covered exactly it (30 issues) — `/Users/joeoakhart/jira-cleanup-20260820/logs/dryrun-all.txt`,\n      `/Users/joeoakhart/jira-cleanup-20260820/logs/final-verify.txt`.\n- [x] [non-codebase] Per issue `len(fetched) == total` held and a backup existed BEFORE any DELETE\n      — `complete=True` everywhere; `backup/<KEY>.json` for all 27 issues with deletions (150MB).\n- [x] [non-codebase] Dry run produced and inspected before `--execute` (`/Users/joeoakhart/jira-cleanup-20260820/logs/dryrun-all.txt`,\n      recorded in full as a ticket comment).\n- [x] [non-codebase] Marker detection ran PRE-STRIP — 30,847 `marked` counted; detection on\n      stripped text would report 0.\n- [x] [non-codebase] Every DELETE honoured `Retry-After` on 429 — 713+ throttles absorbed, 0 failed\n      deletions across 29,931 DELETEs.\n- [x] [non-codebase] Every issue below the cap; REB-1861 5000 -> 79 (`/Users/joeoakhart/jira-cleanup-20260820/logs/final-verify.txt`).\n- [x] [non-codebase] Post-deletion re-fetch shows zero missing distinct bodies and unchanged\n      non-candidate counts, confirmed independently against the backups (MISSING=0 on all 27).\n- [x] [non-codebase] Deletion log has one object per deletion: 29,931 lines in\n      `/Users/joeoakhart/jira-cleanup-20260820/logs/deletions.jsonl`, matching the delete count.\n\nPhase 2 (the 836 truncation-suffix comments) was deliberately NOT executed; it is reported in the\nticket comments as an operator decision, implemented behind `--include-truncated`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787274689538256001,"uuid":"c9eafb3e-c09e-45c8-b548-444fb8b163ff"}